    {
     "kind": "text",
     "text": "More independent, less diverse; aesthetics up too.",
     "rect": [
      60,
      494,
      840,
      34
     ],
     "size": 24,
     "color": "#C00000",
     "align": "center"
    }
   ],
   "speech": "Does it work beyond cherry-picks? Hidden overlays, PASCAL VOC subjects, four styles, 15 minutes on one A100 each. The baseline is vanilla SDXL score distillation; the thesis notes its images bleed into each other. It's not a rival method. Independence is a soft score we made up: each image must pick its own prompt, each prompt its own image, and the score is the weakest match. We win there and on aesthetics, and lose on diversity, since we add constraints. Honestly, style mattered more than our variants, and we never compared against Visual Anagrams, which can't do overlays."
  },
